- actor(a_default, "Default", [...]): The model assigns all nodes to a generic "Default" actor, failing to assign them to "the review clerk" as explicitly identified in the source text.
- action(n1, "start review process"): This action is hallucinated. The source text states the clerk should "start by reviewing the received application", which corresponds to `action(n2, "review received application")`, not an independent starting action.
- action(n12, "end"): This is hallucinated as a separate operational task. The source text "the process will come to an end" dictates the termination of the process, which is correctly represented by `end(e1)` alone.